// This module's path is deliberately nested under the core module's import
// path (github.com/johnewart/pyxis/cmd/llmd), even though it is a
// separate Go module with its own go.mod. Go's "internal" package visibility
// rule is purely textual — a package is importable from anywhere sharing the
// import-path prefix up to the parent of the "internal" segment, regardless
// of module boundaries. Keeping this prefix lets this binary keep importing
// github.com/johnewart/pyxis/internal/... packages after being split into
// its own module.
//
// This binary is llmd's OWN composition root: chat, providers, models, mcp
// (server + upstream proxy), knowledgebase, embedding, search, agent chat
// lifecycle, and tools (the generic framework — toolregistry/toolexec/
// toolsession — with no concrete tool implementations wired in). Knowledge
// storage and embedding are llmd's own (internal/knowledge/*). Workspace
// hosting, dependency-graph services, peer discovery and ingest scheduling are
// not llmd's job: a host that wants those composes them alongside this
// binary's own services.
module github.com/johnewart/pyxis/cmd/llmd

go 1.25.5

require (
	github.com/johnewart/pyxis v0.0.0
	github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3 v1.14.22
)

